## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of schema evolution, per-tenant isolation, versioned data contracts, and end-to-end visibility under partial deployments.

## Key Concepts

- Versioned schemas with schema_version
- Backward/forward compatibility
- Ingest-time shims/transformations
- Region routing by tenant
- Privacy controls

## Code Example

```javascript
function normalizeEvent(raw) {
  const v = raw.schema_version ?? 1;
  if (v === 1) {
    return { tenant_id: raw.tenant_id, event_type: raw.event_type, timestamp: raw.timestamp, payload: raw.payload, session_id: null, latency_ms: null, schema_version: 2 };
  }
  return raw;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for backward compatibility when a deployed app carries mixed-v1 and v2 events?
- What are trade-offs of adding latency_ms at ingestion vs computing it at source?

## Why This Is Asked
Gives a concrete, beginner-friendly OTCA scenario focusing on privacy, sampling, and cross-region streaming.

## Key Concepts
- Deterministic on-device sampling per tenant
- Per-tenant residency and privacy redaction
- Streaming topology and regional storage
- Basic schema design and test strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldSample(tenantId, rate){
  const h = 0|hashCode(tenantId);
  return Math.abs(h) % 100 < rate;
}
function hashCode(s){
  let h=0;
  for(let i=0;i<s.length;i++) h=(h*31+s.charCodeAt(i))|0;
  return h;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to audit privacy without real tenant data?
- How would you handle skewed tenant traffic affecting sampling?

